# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SENSITIVE — never commit anything matched below.
#
# Layered on purpose: named paths first (what we know we produce), then broad
# patterns (what a future change might produce under a name nobody predicted).
# tests/test_secret_hygiene.py enforces this from the other side by failing if
# credential material is ever staged or tracked.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Cloud / service credentials ───────────────────────────────────────────
# The whole directory is ignored rather than individual filenames, so a
# differently-named key file cannot slip through.
secrets/
# GCP service account keys download with the project name and a random hex
# suffix (avapuck-4a3cc0b1102a.json), so match that shape wherever it lands.
*-[0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f][0-9a-f]*.json
*-sa.json
*service-account*.json
*credentials*.json
*client_secret*.json
gcp-*.json
application_default_credentials.json

# ── TLS / key material ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The dev CA and service certs come from scripts/gen_certs.sh, and NONE of it
# is committed -- not even the public certs.
#
# Committing the .crt files while ignoring the .key files was a real trap: a
# fresh clone got three certificates with no matching keys, gen_certs.sh
# refused to overwrite them ("certs/ already populated"), and the IdP died
# with X509: KEY_VALUES_MISMATCH. Every machine generates its own pair.
certs/*.crt
certs/*.key
certs/*.srl
certs/*.cnf
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
*.ppk

# ── Environment files ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Real values live in .env; the committed examples carry placeholders only.
.env
.env.*
.env.local
.env.local.resolved
!.env.example
!.env.local.example

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PIPELINE DATA — regenerated every run, and some of it is sensitive.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# Extracted source data, before any encryption. PLAINTEXT by definition.
data/csv/
# Card prefix/suffix split out of PANs. Middles are encrypted, but the clear
# prefix and suffix are still cardholder data and must not be committed.
data/cards/
# Encrypted Parquet, masked Hive files, generated PDFs.
data/parquet/
data/hive/
data/reports/
# Delivered report copies (scripts/collect_report.sh, and the report stage).
pipeline-reports/

# ── Local state ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
airflow_home/
logs/
*.log
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Airflow standalone writes a generated admin password to disk.
standalone_admin_password.txt
simple_auth_manager_passwords.json.generated

# ── Docker / OS noise ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
docker/volumes/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/
